{
  "manifest_version": "0.1",
  "note": "Existing regression fixtures with human labels attached. `human_label.*` is a person's assessment of the fixture, revisable and not established fact. `regression.deterministic.*` records the deterministic lane's actual output at authoring time, locked for drift detection only -- it is not a correctness claim. `regression.model.*` records which canonical test covers the model-backed lane and what category of behaviour it checks; it carries no severity because that lane is probabilistic and produces nothing lockable. `independent` is false for every entry: this is a hand-built regression set, not an independent benchmark, and no detector threshold, risk mapping, or severity boundary may be tuned to it. Directory and trust analyzers are intentionally absent (no file-based labelled fixtures exist for them yet).",
